<p>That's pretty much spot on.</p>
<p>As for the purpleness: I don't exactly disagree. In part I wanted to keep at least a little of the fever dream aspect that inspired this; mostly it seemed the best way to cram all the references I wanted in there without it being too painfully obvious. It is the weakest part of it, imo. I couldn't find a better way to do it.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Elaboration</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I can see two main approaches to conveying an alien mind through dialog, I call the Kosh and the Kosh2 methods:<br />
Kosh2: Simple, direct statements. Yes. No. Irrelevant. Go here. Do this.<br />
Alien is seeking simplest common reference frame. Communication is objective oriented. Alternately, alien has a machinelike mind.</p>
<p>Kosh: Metaphor and purple prose.<br />
Alien is trying to find common ground despite have different perceptions. Alternately, alien has fey mind. Or is just dicking with you.</p>
<p>-C wants something, yes, but their mind is more on the fey side of the scale. They don't fully understand themselves what they are talking about. Purple seemed the way to go.</p>
<p>One of my original ideas, which can be seen in my sandbox, has a much more personable -C-1 with a more histrionic -D providing the purple bits, with -C-1 explaining as best it could. That ended up being too blunt.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">For&nbsp;reference</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This thing came about when I tried to mount my headcanon on a fever dream I had.<br />
Dream involved a man berating a panda for eating bamboo when they have a carnivorous digestive track, to which the panda replies &quot;So that we endure&quot;. This repeats every thousand years until the heat death of the universe.</p>
<p>The headcanon involves qntm's 001 proposal, 2040, the Pattern Screamers and a bunch of other stuff.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

