<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The first part for me was</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2528 is a network of organic computers spanning most of East and Southeast Asia.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It does say organic, but it also says it is a computer not computer-like, which is where the confusion start. &quot;System of organisms displaying computer-like characteristics&quot; would work better.</p>
<p>Then there's</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2528 is comprised of two primary component organisms: SCP-2528-A, which acts as data storage and network infrastructure, and SCP-2528-B, which enables data processing and environmental manipulation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Which leans a bit too much into the computer simile. I'm no biologist, but I think that you could describe this process without having to compare it to a computer that much.</p>
<p>In general, it isn't really a specific section that causes the confusion, but rather small bits here and there that end up being summed. I would say that describing the SCP as a computer once would suffice to bring in the comparison, and the rest should be descriptions of the organisms as an organism without having to constantly go back to the computer analogy.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<blockquote>
<p>Knowledge regarding the Pattern Screamers shouldn't be required for this. Might reveal some of the easter eggs, but that's all.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well I had no clue what the pattern was until I read the comments. Might have been due to what Decibelles said, the dialogue was pretty dense and loaded, which was rather a slog to read through.</p>

