<p>A couple of minor nitpicks from someone who works with computers for a living:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>These changes then propagate throughout the SCP-2528-A network in a manner closely resembling the activity seen in a distributed data cluster.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This reads to me what &quot;is then eaten in a manner closely resembling the behaviors exhibited by mammals&quot; would to a biologist; it's so strangely non-specific that it comes across as pretty much useless to a professional that actually understands what's being talked about.</p>
<p>Which isn't to say that you should expand on it, maybe the opposite and actually merge it with the sentence before it to read:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>anomalous chemical reactions induce changes to the quantum state<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">s</span> of the entangled particles, <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">that connect back to SCP-2528-A instances</span> thus propagating data throughout the entire cluster.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm also slightly weirded out by the phrase &quot;sapient, data-form intelligences&quot;, as it sounds really technobabble-y to me. Maybe the phrase &quot;sapient entities&quot; would work instead?</p>

