<blockquote>
<p>This reads to me what &quot;is then eaten in a manner closely resembling the behaviors exhibited by mammals&quot; would to a biologist; it's so strangely non-specific that it comes across as pretty much useless to a professional that actually understands what's being talked about.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Fair enough. You have no idea how much time I spent banging my head against that freaking sentence.<br />
For reference, I was specifically thinking of the architecture of a Coherence Cluster.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Which isn't to say that you should expand on it, maybe the opposite and actually merge it with the sentence before it to read:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So don't do, for example</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">this?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>SCP-XXXX-A is comprised of living plants in the clade <em>Bambusoideae Bambusinae</em>. During growth, a shoot of SCP-XXXX-A will anomalously generate particles linked via quantum entanglement throughout its tissues. Several distinct phases of particle generation have been observed.<br />
In the first phase, coinciding with the initial growth of the culm<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-911243-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-911243-1')">1</a></sup>, pairs will form in the rhizome with half of each pair moving into the culm. These particles take up position in the nodes<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-911243-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-911243-2')">2</a></sup> and leaves of the stalk, such that each node and each leaf has at least one connection to the rhizome.<br />
Once the culm has completed growth, entangled particle pairs will begin to form in the areas surrounding rhizome-connecting particles. These particles are organized in such a way as to suggest the structure of a data storage device.<br />
At the same time, the rhizome will begin to generate and share particles with the rhizomes of other instances via anomalous means. This creates a traversable network linking all known instances of SCP-XXXX-A.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX-B is comprised of the species <em>Ailuropoda Melanoleuca</em> and its attendant digestive bacteria.<br />
The metabolic processes of these organisms induce changes to the SCP-XXXX-A network. As a -B instance digests -A matter, anomalous chemical reactions<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-911243-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-911243-3')">3</a></sup> induce changes to the quantum state of the entangled particles being digested<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-911243-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-911243-4')">4</a></sup>. These changes are detected by the connected -A instances, which propagate them through the network.</p>
<p>Most of the entangled particles consumed by an -B instance will excreted during defecation. However some particles will be absorbed into the -A instance's body, where they will generally migrate to the instance's fatty tissues. These particles are theorized to enable control over -B instances.</p>
<p>The decline in the population of <em>Ailuropoda Melanoleuca</em> has resulted in a parallel decline in the processing power available to SCP-XXXX.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I'll admit, &quot;sapient, data-form intelligences&quot; is sort of a guilty pleasure for me. I am currently fighting with myself over keeping it.</p>
